  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5953,
  "title": "Update upload-artifact and download-artifact actions to v4",
  "body": "> The `playground` workflow fails on every push to `main` before its first step: \"This request has been automatically failed because it uses a deprecated version of `actions/upload-artifact: v2`\".\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- 👷🏻 Fixed the `playground` and \"Download localization strings\" workflows failing on deprecated `actions/upload-artifact` versions, in PR [#5953](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5953), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nGitHub rejects `actions/upload-artifact` and `actions/download-artifact` v1–v3, which fails `playground` on every push to `main` and the scheduled \"Download localization strings\" workflow (v3). This moves every remaining v2/v3 use to `@v4`, the tag the other workflows already use.\n\n## Design\n\n- v4 breaking changes do not apply: artifact names are unique within each run, no hidden files are uploaded, and downloads by `name` still extract into `path`.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `playground.yaml`, `samples.07.{a,b,c,d}.*.yaml`: `upload-artifact@v4`\n- `preview-branch.yml`: `upload-artifact@v4` and `download-artifact@v4` (2× each)\n- `download-localization-strings.yml`: `upload-artifact@v4` and `download-artifact@v4`\n\nChecked with `actionlint` (no artifact findings) and a YAML parse. `playground` runs on push to `main`, so it is verified after merge.\n\n- [ ] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
